# Derivatives of expressions that KEEP an fma node.  diff_node() itself has
# always differentiated fma, but simplifying the result sends fma through the
# generic rebuilders (tidy1/close).  With fma missing from IS_OP3 those rebuilt
# a malformed two-operand fma; the workaround skipped simplification entirely.
# Now fma is rebuilt with all three operands, so the derivative is fully
# simplified and still prints correctly.
diff sin(fma(x,x,x))
diff fma(x,x,x)
diff fma(x,y,z)
diff exp(fma(x,x,x))
